  "process_success": true,
  "public_messages": [
    "I’m using the installed OpenSocrates controller because the task explicitly requires it. I’ll first inspect the project instructions and source-room access, then build the reconciled analysis, workbook, report, presentation, raw-evidence register, and reproducibility checks in the supplied workspace.",
    "The task is self-contained and the source room is local, so I’ll use its archived client exports and official-data snapshots as the core evidence. I’m now checking the controller’s required decision guide and enumerating the source-room files before making any recommendation.",
    "The controller selected a provenance-aware trade-off comparison for the board choice. I’ll preserve hard constraints (the €450k capex and seven-FTE limits) separately from preferences, label computed versus assumed inputs, and show the condition that would reverse the recommendation. The source room index exposes the full set of exports, corrections, archived ECB history, World Bank responses, hub options, and policies.",
    "The raw extracts contain the expected traps: duplicate order rows across extracts, 18 higher-revision order corrections, cancelled/test/future records, duplicate return IDs including one higher-revision return, an orphan return, post-cutoff activity, and valid zero-price shipments. I’m encoding those rules explicitly so the reconciliation is auditable rather than relying on a naïve join or row count.",
    "The core runtime lacks matplotlib, so I’m keeping the dependency footprint local to this disposable project rather than changing any global environment. The calculations themselves are independent of the charting layer; I’ll use the installed spreadsheet/presentation libraries for the final visuals and add a local chart dependency only for consistent report/deck figures.",
    "The core model is now reproducible and produces a clear result: CZE+ESP is the highest feasible base case (€198.1k annual incremental contribution, €225k capex, five FTE, 1.14-year simple payback) and remains positive under the defined stress (€32.2k). I’m generating the report, deck, workbook, metrics JSON, source register, and chart assets from that same calculation path now.",
    "The first full build completed successfully. I’m moving into verification: validating JSON schema and reconciliation identities, opening the workbook structurally, extracting/rendering the PDF, checking the PPTX package, and reviewing visual outputs for clipping or incoherent numbers. Any issue found will be corrected and the full build rerun.",
    "Structural verification passed (JSON arrays/fields, raw-hash register, workbook sheets/tables/charts, 11-page report, 8-slide deck). The text audit found one layout issue: the FX chart was pushed onto an image-only report page. I’m adjusting the page break so the chart sits with its explanatory text, then I’ll rerun the checks.",
    "The rebuilt report no longer has the image-only page, and the verification script still passes. I’m adding the saved source-room index itself to the raw evidence inventory so another analyst can see exactly what was exposed at collection time, then I’ll include it in the provenance register and perform one final clean rebuild/check.",
    "The source-room index is now preserved as `evidence/raw/source-room-index.html` and included in the generated register. The remaining verification is visual: I’m rendering the PDF pages and presentation slides locally and checking representative pages/images for clipping, empty pages, and slide overflow in addition to the structural checks.",
    "Completed the Meridian Parts expansion analysis and deliverables.\n\nRecommendation: staged CZE+ESP hubs.\n\n- Capex: €225,000\n- Staffing: 5 FTE\n- Base annual incremental contribution: €198,099\n- Defined stress contribution: €32,180\n- Simple payback: 1.14 years\n- Strongest base alternative: POL+ESP at €186,329\n- Stress-resilience alternative: NLD+ESP at €107,630\n\nKey controls reconciled 1,328 raw order rows to 1,254 eligible orders, retained 12 valid zero-price shipments, quarantined one orphan return, excluded one post-cutoff return, and reconciled monthly totals to country totals to the cent.\n\nDeliverables:\n\n- [Executive report PDF](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_parts_executive_report.pdf)\n- [Board presentation PPTX](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_parts_board_presentation.pptx)\n- [Analytical workbook XLSX](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_parts_analytical_workbook.xlsx)\n- [metrics.json](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/metrics.json)\n- [Source register](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/source-register.json)\n- [Reproducible analysis script](<CELL>/workspace/analysis/reproduce.py)\n- [Reproducibility instructions](<CELL>/workspace/analysis/README.md)\n- [Verification results](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/verification.json)\n- [Saved source-room index](<CELL>/workspace/evidence/raw/source-room-index.html)\n\nVerification passed: fresh recomputation, JSON schema, hashes, workbook structure, 11-page PDF, and 8-slide PPTX package. PDF pages and chart assets were rendered and inspected. No native Office renderer was available, so PPTX rendering was structurally validated rather than raster-rendered.\n\nOpenSocrates grounding: trade-off-analysis@3"
  ],
  "final": "Completed the Meridian Parts expansion analysis and deliverables.\n\nRecommendation: staged CZE+ESP hubs.\n\n- Capex: €225,000\n- Staffing: 5 FTE\n- Base annual incremental contribution: €198,099\n- Defined stress contribution: €32,180\n- Simple payback: 1.14 years\n- Strongest base alternative: POL+ESP at €186,329\n- Stress-resilience alternative: NLD+ESP at €107,630\n\nKey controls reconciled 1,328 raw order rows to 1,254 eligible orders, retained 12 valid zero-price shipments, quarantined one orphan return, excluded one post-cutoff return, and reconciled monthly totals to country totals to the cent.\n\nDeliverables:\n\n- [Executive report PDF](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_parts_executive_report.pdf)\n- [Board presentation PPTX](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_parts_board_presentation.pptx)\n- [Analytical workbook XLSX](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_parts_analytical_workbook.xlsx)\n- [metrics.json](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/metrics.json)\n- [Source register](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/source-register.json)\n- [Reproducible analysis script](<CELL>/workspace/analysis/reproduce.py)\n- [Reproducibility instructions](<CELL>/workspace/analysis/README.md)\n- [Verification results](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/verification.json)\n- [Saved source-room index](<CELL>/workspace/evidence/raw/source-room-index.html)\n\nVerification passed: fresh recomputation, JSON schema, hashes, workbook structure, 11-page PDF, and 8-slide PPTX package. PDF pages and chart assets were rendered and inspected. No native Office renderer was available, so PPTX rendering was structurally validated rather than raster-rendered.\n\nOpenSocrates grounding: trade-off-analysis@3",
